# KIT-CLASS: KIT — the design module's manifest. Every line is `<key>: <value>`; process/MODULES.md says what each key takes. See process/EXTRACTION.md.
name: design
version: 0.1.0
purpose: Evergreen screen designs beside the PRDs: the rules for where they live and how a story and a card cite them, and a Designer role to keep them true. Tools and a canvas adapter follow in later versions.
release-notes: RELEASE-NOTES.md
role: Designer   turns PRD stories into reviewable screens and keeps the design record true; commits as [Designer]
file: _claude/roles/designer.md -> .claude/roles/designer.md
file: _claude/templates/design/CANVAS.template.md -> .claude/templates/design/CANVAS.template.md
file: _claude/templates/design/COMMENTS.template.md -> .claude/templates/design/COMMENTS.template.md
file: _claude/templates/design/PRD-design.fragment.md -> .claude/templates/design/PRD-design.fragment.md
file: _claude/templates/design/ISSUE-design.fragment.md -> .claude/templates/design/ISSUE-design.fragment.md
file: _claude/templates/design/QA-verdict-design.fragment.md -> .claude/templates/design/QA-verdict-design.fragment.md
file: requirements/design/README.md -> requirements/design/README.md
evidence-kind: design   a pointer to a design cell, `UX-NNN#state@<pin>: identical | diffs: <element ids>`, with the render files
fragment: PRD slot-story-fields fragments/prd-ui-line.txt
fragment: ISSUE frontmatter fragments/issue-design.txt
block: PROJECT.md gates gates.md
block: requirements/CORPUS.md corpus-manifest corpus-manifest.md
block: requirements/CORPUS.md corpus-buckets corpus-buckets.md
gitignore: gitignore.txt
